{
  "about": "THE RECIPES (vllm_lb/catalog.py `document`): how each model is launched, independent of hardware — its engine and build (the image is the matrix's, library/images), parsers, speculative decoding, KV dtype, engine flags. `overrides.<accelerator>` holds the few settings that apply only on that accelerator (DeepSeek-V4's B12X kernels on the GB10).",
  "recipes": [
    {
      "model": "qwen3.8-flash-next-hibrid48",
      "node_engine": "vllm",
      "launch": {
        "cluster": {
          "default": true,
          "build": "fleet",
          "kv_cache_dtype": "fp8_e4m3",
          "kv_cache_dtype_backend": {
            "name": "QWEN4_EXP_QSA_TRITON",
            "reads": [
              "bfloat16",
              "fp8",
              "fp8_e4m3",
              "nvfp4"
            ],
            "source": "models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/qsa.py in myllmbox/qwen38-flash-next-cluster-vllm:v5 (read on box-a 2026-10-26, no engine started): Qwen4ExpQSAFlashAttentionBackend (get_name QWEN4_EXP_QSA_TRITON) supported_kv_cache_dtypes auto, bfloat16, fp8, fp8_e4m3, nvfp4; supports_kv_cache_dtype: 'The QSA main cache is only read by the Triton kernel in ops/qsa.py, which dequantizes in registers, so the FlashAttention capability is irrelevant here' - nvfp4 has its own page geometry, writer and read kernel there; the MTP drafter's attentions are QSA too (mtp.py _iter_qsa_attentions). Anything else raises 'Qwen4Exp QSA requires a BF16, FP8-E4M3 or NVFP4 main KV cache' (qsa.py:437; generations 262/265 at int4_per_token_head). NVFP4 NOT MEASURED on this fleet"
          },
          "tool_call_parser": "qwen3_xml",
          "reasoning_parser": "qwen3",
          "speculative_config": {
            "method": "mtp",
            "num_speculative_tokens": 4
          },
          "gpu_memory_utilization": 0.7,
          "kv_cache_memory": 28000000000,
          "ple_replicate": false,
          "mtp_prefix": "mtp."
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "model": "qwen3.8-flash-next-sglang",
      "launch": {
        "cluster": {
          "engine": "sglang",
